From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Giuseppe Maggio <jertlok@proton.me>
Date: Sun, 23 Aug 2026 12:10:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: ath10k: don't wait for DISABLE_KEY acks WCN3990 never
 sends

ath10k_install_key() waits 3 s for the firmware to acknowledge every
key command. Measured on a Pixel 2 XL (WCN3990 hw1.0): the DISABLE_KEY
ack never arrives on any teardown leg - disconnect, roam or the
pre-suspend teardown cfg80211 performs for a driver suspending without
WoWLAN - even with the wait extended to 8 s, while the firmware
carries on normally. The wait only stalls the wiphy for 3 s per key at
suspend entry and on every roam. Send the command and return; SET_KEY
keeps its wait and its recovery escalation.

Signed-off-by: Giuseppe Maggio <jertlok@proton.me>
---
 drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath10k/mac.c | 13 +++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 13 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath10k/mac.c b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath10k/mac.c
index 94fddd8094eb..830822566ffe 100644
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath10k/mac.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath10k/mac.c
@@ -324,6 +324,19 @@ static int ath10k_install_key(struct ath10k_vif *arvif,
 	if (ret)
 		return ret;
 
+	/*
+	 * WCN3990 does not acknowledge DISABLE_KEY on a teardown: measured
+	 * on a Pixel 2 XL across every disconnect, roam and pre-suspend
+	 * teardown - the ack never arrives even after 8 s, and the firmware
+	 * carries on normally.  Waiting only stalls the wiphy for 3 s per
+	 * key at suspend entry and on every roam.  Fire and forget; a stray
+	 * late ack cannot confuse a later SET_KEY wait because none was
+	 * ever observed on this firmware, and reinit_completion() above
+	 * clears anything pending before each new command.
+	 */
+	if (cmd == DISABLE_KEY)
+		return 0;
+
 	time_left = wait_for_completion_timeout(&ar->install_key_done, 3 * HZ);
 	if (time_left == 0) {
 		/* An unacknowledged SET_KEY leaves a link that is meant to
